Runtime Analysis (RASP/IAST) in CI/CD
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

• Understand the concepts of Interactive Application Security Testing (IAST) and Runtime Application Self-Protection (RASP) • Set up a complete DevSecOps pipeline with integrated security testing • Configure and deploy open-source IAST tools for runtime vulnerability detection • Implement RASP capabilities using open-source solutions • Integrate security testing into CI/CD workflows • Analyze and interpret runtime security findings • Apply security remediation strategies based on runtime analysis results

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

• Basic understanding of Linux command line operations • Familiarity with Docker and containerization concepts • Knowledge of CI/CD pipeline fundamentals • Understanding of web application security basics • Experience with Git version control system • Basic knowledge of YAML configuration files

